Z||000002||grinthock||09-02-2001||09:28 AM||||Yes sir-eee that was Jay indeed, did you miss the 32V Northstar logo on the rear bumper?  (small, cute actually).<P><BR>His car can be seen from a fair ways, with those cool exhaust tips he's running.  Oh and the sound of it....<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroworldbanner.gif"> </A> <BR>Fieroworld!  Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||09-02-2001||05:10 PM||||Hey, yes that was me on the way back from Cayuga.  I was dead tired and could barely keep my eyes open!  Nightime racing will do that to you.  I saw the thumbs up <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Thought you were egging me on for a highway race!  I usually don't on the street, especially on a long week-end.  Come over and see me at the show!<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
